  "starterCode": "def hit_rate_at_k(recommendations: list, ground_truth: list, k: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the fraction of users with a relevant item in their first k recommendations.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write code here\n    pass",
  "createdAt": "2026-01-31T22:50:42.552Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-08-23T21:27:32.305Z",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nProportion of search or recommendation queries where at least one ground-truth item was surfaced in top $k$.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef hit_rate_at_k(recommendations: list, ground_truth: list, k: int) -> float:\n    hits = 0\n    n = len(recommendations)\n    for recs, actual in zip(recommendations, ground_truth):\n        top_k = set(recs[:k])\n        if any(item in top_k for item in actual):\n            hits += 1\n    return round(hits / n, 4) if n > 0 else 0.0\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization:** Prepares parameters into optimized NumPy arrays or native data structures for uniform batch computation.\n2. **Vectorized Core:** Executes mathematical transformations in SIMD fashion to eliminate slow Python iteration overhead.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Applies clipping and numerical stabilization to prevent floating-point anomalies (such as $\\log(0)$ or zero division).\n",
